-- title:
--   Edge certificate data at height 1000000
-- statement:
--   Certificate data for the horizontal argument change of $\zeta$ along the segment $\sigma\in[-1,2]$ at height $t=10^6$.
--
--   One record of the framework structure `Arb4.EdgeD`: the height, the Euler–Maclaurin cut $N=300000$, a log bound $L$, 73 octant pieces (`Arb4.PieceD`: a centre, a radius, an octant label, Taylor and remainder budgets) with breakpoints from $\sigma=2$ to $\sigma=-1$, two endpoint boxes and the final enclosure $[Lo,Hi]$ of the argument change. The data were produced by a program and are not trusted; each piece is checked by the kernel in `RHX1000000.Edge.piece_00` … `piece_72`, the rest in `RHX1000000.Edge.rest`.
-- source:
--   Computational certificate extending the kernel-checked verification of the Riemann hypothesis on prove2.me (published ArdaRH65K framework, Proved to height 65000; extended to height 100000 by the RHX100000 problems) to height 1000000; data produced by an exact integer Rust port of the framework checkers and checked by the Lean kernel.

